---
title: Uses card
description: A thing you own and recommend — the shot, the vendor, why you like it, what it cost, and the disclosure as its own row. It is the affiliate card, and nothing about it is new.
eyebrow: Collections · Uses
source: src/components/ad.css
---
<p>The uses collection did not need a card of its own: <code>im-affiliate</code> from <a href="/components/ads/#affiliate-product-card">Ads &amp; sponsors</a> already holds everything one needs. This page is the card in the context it is actually used in.</p>

<h2>The card</h2>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-affiliates">
	{{#each demo.uses}}{{#match @index "<" 2}}
	<article class="im-affiliate">
		<span class="im-affiliate-media"><img src="{{lookup ../demo.shots @index}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span>
		<a class="im-affiliate-name" href="/collections/uses/page/" rel="sponsored noopener">{{name}}</a>
		<p class="im-affiliate-by">{{by}}</p>
		<p class="im-affiliate-text">{{text}}</p>
		<p class="im-affiliate-meta"><span class="im-affiliate-price">{{price}}</span>{{#if was}}<span class="im-affiliate-was">{{was}}</span>{{/if}}<span class="im-badge im-badge-success">Still using it</span></p>
		<div class="im-affiliate-actions"><a class="im-btn im-btn-primary im-btn-sm" href="#the-card" rel="sponsored noopener">Where I got it {{icon "arrow-up-right"}}</a><a class="im-btn im-btn-sm" href="/collections/uses/page/">Why this one</a></div>
		<p class="im-affiliate-note">Affiliate link — I earn a little if you buy, at no cost to you</p>
	</article>
	{{/match}}{{/each}}
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Two tiers, not one</h2>
<p>Four things you would fight for get a card each. The other twenty go in the <a href="/components/widgets/#things-i-use">products widget</a> as rows — a name, what it is for, and an arrow. A page of twenty-four equal cards says everything matters equally, which is never true and is not what a reader came to find out.</p>
{{#example style="max-width: 24rem"}}
<section class="im-widget">
	<h2 class="im-widget-title">Small things</h2>
	<div class="im-widget-products">
		{{#each demo.products}}
		<a class="im-widget-product" href="#two-tiers-not-one"><span class="im-widget-product-mark">{{name.[0]}}</span><span class="im-widget-product-name">{{name}}</span><span class="im-widget-product-note">{{note}}</span>{{icon "arrow-up-right"}}</a>
		{{/each}}
	</div>
</section>
{{/example}}

<h2>The disclosure is part of the card</h2>
<p><code>im-affiliate-note</code> is a row of its own at the bottom, above a rule, in the same mono as every other label in the system — so a reader who has learnt what that type means on an <a href="/components/ads/">ad</a> knows what it means here without being told twice.</p>
<p>It is <strong>not</strong> the page's disclosure. That goes at the top, in a <a href="/components/callout/">callout</a>, before the list: the note on a card is a reminder, and the callout is the actual statement.</p>

<h2>Rules</h2>
<ul>
	<li><strong>Own it, or take it off.</strong> A uses page listing things you have not used is an ad page with a different name.</li>
	<li><strong>Say when it was last checked.</strong> A three-year-old recommendation for a discontinued product is worse than no page.</li>
	<li><strong><code>rel="sponsored noopener"</code> on every paid link</strong> — the machine-readable half of what the card already says in words.</li>
</ul>
